{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.FrakDEnergyDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.FrakDEnergyDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Hom.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Cast.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Invertible","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Function.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.frakD_is_pure_emitted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.frakD_is_pure_emitted","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frakD-energy-decomposition.lean#L110-L119","doc":"**The 𝔇 reinterpretation.** If the deuteron unit is a bar-odd energy\n`E_unit = U` with `U` bar-odd (`σ U = -U` — the width datum `ℏ/𝔇` lives in\nthe emitted/sinh sector), then `E_unit` equals its own emitted part and\nhas zero retained part: it is a *purely decay-channel* energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.oddPart_eq_zero_iff_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.oddPart_eq_zero_iff_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frakD-energy-decomposition.lean#L95-L108","doc":"**Pure-binding criterion.** The emitted (bar-skew) channel vanishes iff\n`E` is bar-even: a nucleus radiates no γγ̄ / carries no 𝔇 channel exactly\nwhen its binding is purely retained. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.even_add_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.even_add_odd","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frakD-energy-decomposition.lean#L87-L93","doc":"**Reconstruction.** `E = retained E + emitted E`: every energy is its\nbar-even binding part plus its bar-odd decay part. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:frakD-energy-decomposition","label":"prop:frakD-energy-decomposition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frakD-energy-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.oddPart_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.oddPart_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frakD-energy-decomposition.lean#L78-L83","doc":"The emitted part is bar-odd: `σ(emitted E) = −emitted E` — the sinh /\ndecay-width channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.evenPart_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.evenPart_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frakD-energy-decomposition.lean#L71-L75","doc":"The retained part is bar-even: `σ(retained E) = retained E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.oddPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.oddPart","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frakD-energy-decomposition.lean#L63-L65","doc":"Bar-odd (\"emitted\", sinh — the bar-skew channel P_skew) projection\n`(E − σE)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.evenPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.evenPart","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frakD-energy-decomposition.lean#L60-L61","doc":"Bar-even (\"retained\", cosh) projection `(E + σE)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.map_invOf_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrakD.map_invOf_two","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frakD-energy-decomposition.lean#L48-L58","doc":"A ring endomorphism fixes `⅟2`: it fixes `2`, so `σ(⅟2)` is a left\ninverse of `2` and hence *is* `⅟2`.  (The analogue of `map_div₀` /\n`map_ofNat` for the `Invertible` halving.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}